</span></span><!--[endif]-->Research report summarizing results of the pilot
test, lessons learned, – ATP + 12months.<o:p></o:p></div></div><div><br></div><div><b><br></b></div><div><b>Results:</b></div><div>
<div>The results from the literature review, interviews, and the pilot
study generated a report that helped future developers and researchers better
understand when and how XR technologies are applied and when they should be
avoided in hardware system verification and validation. Results from the
literature review and SME interviews produced XR Verification Decision
Framework. It is the first draft for NASA to make decisions on program
requirements regarding XR technologies. The framework is the foundation for
identifying gaps in research. The PI team created a VR duplicate of a
high-fidelity physical mockup, the Habitable Airlock. Outcomes were observed to
be about the same for both mockups with two exceptions. The appropriateness of
VR mockups relative to a PR mockup was evaluated, but it is both resource
intensive and impractical for NASA partners. PR and VR mockup for two
verification-like tasks were compared, Hand Signal Identification and Field of
View. These results support the cautious conclusion from phase 1, that VR might
be best suited for demonstrations.<br></div></div>
